# A Unit scrutinee on the v2 JS codegen

`BUGS.md` `js-v2-unit-pattern-does-not-match-and-unit-literal-pattern-crashes`. Two defects, one
scrutinee. The unit value is `null` on the v2 JS lane, and the emitted matcher read `.t` off it
unconditionally, so `case () =>` raised
`TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 't')` — **a pattern match crashing on a value it
simply does not match.** The same unguarded read was in both "no arm matched" error messages, so the
diagnostic for a failed match crashed too, precisely where a diagnostic was wanted.

Separately, `$isTag` began `!!(v && …)`, and `null` is falsy, so `case _: Unit` could never hold.
Same shape as the interpreter and the v1 JS backend, both fixed earlier the same day: a type-test
table listing every type *except* this one.

```scalascript
def viaAscription(x: Any): String = x match
  case _: Unit => "UNIT"
  case _ => "OTHER"

def viaLiteral(x: Any): String = x match
  case () => "UNIT"
  case _ => "OTHER"

println("ascription-unit: " + viaAscription(println("")))
println("literal-unit:    " + viaLiteral(println("")))
println("ascription-int:  " + viaAscription(5))
println("literal-int:     " + viaLiteral(5))
```

**`jvm` and `js` are deliberately absent, and the reason is a second defect this case cannot pin.**
Measured on all five lanes, `case ()` splits them two against two:

| lane | `case ()` on the unit value |
|---|---|
| `jvm` (real Scala) | `UNIT` |
| `js` (v1 backend) | `UNIT` |
| `int` | `OTHER` |
| native / v2 | `OTHER` |
| v2 JS | crashed; now `OTHER` |

So `UNIT` is the right answer and half the lanes give it. That is a real cross-lane divergence, filed
as `unit-literal-pattern-diverges-two-lanes-against-two`, and fixing it means touching pattern
lowering on the lanes that are wrong — a different change from this one, with goldens at stake.
`js` is therefore DECLARED KNOWN-RED rather than excluded, and that distinction is the point: taking
it out of `backends:` also removes the **`JS/v2` lane, which is the one this case exists to gate** —
`also-codegen: v2` runs the v2 codegen through the js lane's declaration. A case that stops
exercising the code it was written for is worse than no case, so the divergent lane keeps running
and diffing under its own bucket. `jvm` stays out because the v2 codegen has no jvm-side variant
here to gate.

This case pins: **no crash, and agreement with the lane the v2 JS codegen is supposed to mirror.**

The two non-unit lines are the guard that the fix did not make everything match: a `null`-safe read
must still let an ordinary scrutinee reach the ordinary arms.
